From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:49:50 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] android: backing store that hands its pixels to the
 compositor as a graphics buffer

With the stock QRhiBackingStore the compositor uploads from a shared copy of the
backing store QImage, which the upload batch keeps until the frame's resources
are released, so the next QPainter::begin() deep-copies the whole window image
(15-20 MB per repaint on phone and tablet screens).  Offer the image as a
QPlatformGraphicsBuffer instead: the compositor then wraps the raw pixels
without taking a reference.  Used together with the KiCad port's binary patch
that drops the compositor's own detach of the uploaded image.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PMkXiZQmqtvCJRtsVHJjyT
